# Agent runtime env — platform-managed deployment.
#
# WHO WRITES THIS FILE
#   The platform control-plane writes this file during "materialize":
#     POST /api/agents/<id>/materialize
#   It scans the current agent.yaml for every `*_env` reference
#   (models.targets[*].api_key_env, mcp_servers[*].api_key_env,
#    connectors.*.*_env, embedding.*_env, rerank.*_env,
#    knowledge connectors *_env) and emits one KEY= line per reference,
#   preserving any values already filled in by the operator.
#
# HOW TO FILL VALUES
#   Option A — Admin console: open the Agent's "Required secrets" panel;
#               it shows every KEY= and lets you paste values in the browser.
#   Option B — Direct edit: after materialize writes the stub, edit this file
#               manually and restart the agent process.
#
# NAMING CONVENTION FOR *_env REFERENCES IN agent.yaml
#   Model API keys     : FLEETENT_MODEL_<ROLE>_API_KEY   (e.g. _PRIMARY_, _FAST_)
#   Embedding          : FLEETENT_EMBED_<FIELD>           (e.g. _API_KEY, _ENDPOINT)
#   Rerank             : FLEETENT_RERANK_<FIELD>
#   Slack connector    : <AGENT>_SLACK_BOT / <AGENT>_SLACK_APP
#   MCP server         : <SERVER_ID>_MCP_TOKEN / <SERVER_ID>_DSN
#   Knowledge (GDrive) : <AGENT>_GD_ACCESS_TOKEN / _REFRESH_TOKEN / _CLIENT_ID / _SECRET
#   Knowledge (Conf.)  : <AGENT>_CONF_USERNAME / <AGENT>_CONF_TOKEN
#
# Secrets are NEVER inlined in agent.yaml. Never commit this file with real values.
# For standalone (no-platform) deployment see: config/agent/.env.standalone.example
